{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB11063 - MONDO_948",
  "verbalization": "Polysorbate 80 is implicated in the pathogenesis of Xerophthalmia through off-label use in conjunction with other substances that share a common mechanism of action. The evidence suggests that Polysorbate 80, when used off-label, is associated with Sjogren Syndrome, a condition characterized by dry eyes and mouth, which in turn is linked to Xerophthalmia. This chain of associations is supported by the off-label use of Polysorbate 80 in combination with Povidone K30 and Propylene Glycol, all of which are indicated for Xerophthalmia. The shared mechanism of action involves the potential to disrupt mucosal hydration and immune function, which may contribute to the development of dry eye and dry mouth, leading to the clinical manifestations of Xerophthalmia. The integrated evidence highlights a potential mechanistic link between Polysorbate 80 and Xerophthalmia through its role in exacerbating conditions that affect mucosal hydration and immune response.",
